      "cve": "CVE-2026-116271",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-116271"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "MIME::Parser::FileUnder versions before 5.521 for Perl reuse a pre-created output directory and follow symlinks in it, letting local users redirect attachment writes.\n\nEach message is written to a directory named msg-\u003ctime\u003e-\u003cpid\u003e-\u003cn\u003e under the output base, and an existing directory of that name is used as is. A file name counts as unused when nothing exists at that path, which holds for a dangling symlink, and the body file is then opened in a way that follows the link.\n\nWhen the output base is writable by other users, as with output_under(\"/tmp\"), a local user can pre-create the directory with a symlink named like an attachment. The parser then writes the attachment to the link target with the privileges of the parsing process.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
