          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-116273"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "MIME::Parser versions before 5.521 for Perl set no limit on the number of message parts by default, allowing memory exhaustion.\n\nThe max_parts option defaulted to -1, which disables the limit, so a parser created with default settings builds an entity for every part however many a message has.\n\nVersion 5.521 sets max_parts to 1000 and max_depth to 64 by default. Setting either to -1 still removes the limit.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
